# Pentatonic Across the Neck (repertoire plan: st-pent-connect). An original 16-bar melody in
# A minor pentatonic that climbs through the five boxes and comes back down, with the box numbers
# of the Scales screen: box 5 (frets 2-5) in bars 1-2, box 1 (frets 5-8) in bars 3-4, box 2
# (frets 7-10) in bars 5-6, box 3 (frets 9-13) in bar 7, box 4 (frets 12-15) at the top in bars
# 8-9, then box 3 (bar 10), box 2 (bars 11-12), box 1 (bars 13-14) and home to box 5 (bars 15-16).
# Every move to the next box is a slide: going up, the ring finger slides two frets (or three) and
# lands where the new box puts it; coming down, the index finger slides back.
# Bars 17-32 play the same notes over a C chord, where they sound as C major pentatonic. Only the
# very last note changes: the tune comes home to A over Am7 and to C over C.
# Notes on beats 1 and 3 are C, E or G (in both chords) or a step from one, so both halves sound settled.
title: Pentatonic Across the Neck
composer: Sixstring Academy
source: Original study in A minor and C major pentatonic, all five boxes
licence: Original study for Sixstring Academy
difficulty: 6
tags: minor pentatonic, major pentatonic, five boxes, slides, whole neck
tempo: 88
time: 4/4
key: Am

